  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Acoustic cavitation can bridge a ~4 orders-of-magnitude temperature gap from demonstrated sonoluminescence (~16,000 K) to D-D thermonuclear conditions (~10⁸ K)",
      "D-D fusion gain Q ≥ ~3.5 is achievable in collapsing bubbles to enable net-positive electrical output",
      "Acoustic driver wall-plug efficiency η_driver ≈ 85% is attainable in a reactor-scale piezoelectric system (vs. only Kp ≥ 55% material coupling demonstrated)",
      "Acoustic driver power can scale ~6,250× from the largest commercial unit (16 kW Hielscher UIP16000) to ~100 MW per module while preserving the cavitation regime",
      "Fusion energy thermalizes in the deuterated liquid medium, enabling a conventional Rankine/sCO2 thermal cycle at ~35% efficiency",
      "PZT transducers retain performance and acceptable lifetime under D-D neutron irradiation in a commercial reactor",
      "D₂O (or deuterated acetone) supply chains can sustain commercial-scale operation given India+Canada hold ~80% of global D₂O exports"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Plasma confinement coils / HTS magnets and cryoplant (CAS 220103 → $0)",
      "Tritium breeding blanket and tritium supply infrastructure (CAS 220106 eliminated; D-D fuel cycle)",
      "RF / NBI auxiliary plasma heating systems (CAS 220104 → $0)",
      "Direct energy conversion subsystem (CAS 220109 → $0; thermalization in liquid medium)",
      "High-energy laser drivers, optics, and multi-kJ pulsed energy stores (vs. laser ICF)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Piezoelectric ultrasonic transducer array at reactor scale (CAS 220107 ≈ $42.5M/module) with neutron-irradiation qualification",
      "D₂O vessel and liquid fill — ~113 m³ per module at $300–$475/kg, ~$56M D₂O fill per module + ~$71M vessel",
      "D₂O circulation, management, and tritium-byproduct separation systems (~$72M/module combined)",
      "Periodic transducer replacement under neutron flux (~$6.2M/yr levelized, ~2 replacements over 40 yr plant life)",
      "Heavy-water coolant loop to steam generator (~$195M plant-wide CAS 220200)"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Foundational physics undemonstrated: ~4 orders-of-magnitude temperature gap between sonoluminescence (~16,000 K) and D-D fusion (~10⁸ K) with no published theoretical mechanism to bridge it",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No reactor design, vessel geometry, shielding concept, or energy conversion pathway has been published — entire CAS22 cost basis is speculative",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Acoustic driver wall-plug efficiency η_driver = 85% is unsupported; only Kp ≥ 55% planar coupling is measured. At η_driver = 0.55, breakeven Q rises from ~3.5 to ~5.2 (50% increase)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "100 MW/module acoustic driver is ~6,250× larger than the largest commercial unit (16 kW); Q and acoustic power are coupled unknowns, so the sensitivity sweep at fixed Q=10 is physically unjustified",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Scientific reputational overhang from the 2008 Taleyarkhan misconduct finding has eliminated community consensus and research funding, blocking independent replication and theoretical work",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "D-D neutron flux (~50% of reactions yield 2.45 MeV neutrons) drives substantial shielding/activation requirements with no published engineering analysis",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Neutron-irradiation lifetime of PZT piezoelectric transducers is unstudied; transducer replacement cadence and cost are unknown at reactor scale",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "D₂O supply concentration: India + Canada account for ~80% of global D₂O exports by value, creating geographic supply risk for commercial deployment",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "description": "Conditional LCOE shows plant availability (|ε|=0.95), WACC (|ε|=0.93), and thermal efficiency (|ε|=0.72) dominate over Q (|ε|=0.53) — financing and heat-cycle risks rival physics risk if viability is achieved",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Regulatory classification (nuclear vs. non-nuclear) for a novel acoustic fusion concept is undefined and could materially extend licensing timeline",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
